  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward bias when recent history shows volatility followed by a spike; true outcomes often reverse direction immediately after the model's peak.",
    "When sentiment shifts from negative (-1.0) to positive (1.0), the model overestimates the magnitude of the subsequent rally, failing to account for mean reversion.",
    "The model fails to capture high-frequency volatility spikes within the 30-day horizon, instead smoothing them into a linear trend that misses extreme highs and lows.",
    "In periods of low sentiment (0.0), the model assumes stability but true outcomes frequently exhibit sudden reversals or sharp drops not reflected in the forecast.",
    "The model consistently underestimates the depth of corrections following a positive sentiment spike, resulting in forecasts that remain elevated while prices drop."
  ]
